.TH FANTICS 1
.SH NAME
fantics \- staged-performance player (timed reveal/emphasis/pause)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dreammachines/fantics
.RI [ script.fant ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Fantics
is a work-alike of Nelson's own term, from
.IR "Computer Lib/Dream Machines" ,
for the craft of how information is staged for a person \(em pacing,
emphasis, the dramatic pause \(em as a real design discipline in its
own right, not a technology. It plays back a script of timed "beats"
with real elapsed-time pacing on a black stage.
.PP
.I Script.fant
defaults to
.BR /lib/fantics/demo.fant .
A script is a sequence of beats:
.IP
.nf
.ft L
TYPE ms
<text, revealed one character at a time, ms between each>
END

FLASH ms
<text, shown all at once, held for ms before advancing>
END

PAUSE ms
END
.ft
.fi
.PP
.B PAUSE
shows nothing at all for its duration \(em the beat
.I is
the silence, Nelson's dramatic pause taken literally.
.PP
Space or Return skips the current beat's animation (or advances if it
is already fully revealed);
.B r
restarts from the first beat;
.B q
or Escape quits.
.SH FILES
.TF /lib/fantics/demo.fant
.TP
.B /lib/fantics/demo.fant
A short performance about fantics itself, using the technique to
explain the technique.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/dreammachines/fantics.b
